# Book Management REST API — Educational Implementation

## Overview

This project implements a fully functional RESTful API for managing books using **Node.js** with the **Express.js** framework. The design follows standard HTTP conventions (GET for reads, POST for creation, PUT for full updates, DELETE for removal) and uses an in-memory array as storage so you can run it immediately without setting up a database. Every function is documented with JSDoc comments, custom error classes are used throughout, and the code is organized into logical sections to demonstrate good separation of concerns.

---

## File 1: `package.json`

```json
{
  "name": "book-management-api",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Educational REST API for managing books using Node.js and Express.js",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js",
    "dev": "nodemon server.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.18.2"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "nodemon": "^3.0.1"
  }
}
```

**Why this structure?** `package.json` declares our dependencies and scripts. We use `express` as the web framework and `nodemon` in dev to auto-restart the server on file changes — a common productivity pattern in Node.js development.

