```markdown
# 📚 Book Management REST API

An educational REST API built with **Node.js** and **Express.js** that demonstrates CRUD operations, filtering, validation, error handling, and statistics endpoints.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js >= 18.x
- npm (comes with Node.js)

## Installation & Running

```bash
# Clone or navigate to the project directory
npm install          # Install dependencies
npm start            # Start the server on port 3000
```

For development with auto-reload:
```bash
npm run dev
```

The API will be available at **http://localhost:3000**

---

## Endpoints & Example Requests

### GET /books — List all books (with optional filters)

```bash
# Get all books
curl http://localhost:3000/books

# Filter by genre
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?genre=fiction"

# Filter by author name substring
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?author=hawking"

# Minimum rating filter
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?minRating=4.5"

# Books published after a year
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?publishedYearAfter=1950"
```

### GET /books/:id — Get a single book

```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/books/1
```

### POST /books — Create a new book

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "1984",
    "author": "George Orwell",
    "genre": "Dystopian",
    "publishedYear": 1949,
    "rating": 4.7
  }'
```

### PUT /books/:id — Full update of a book

```bash
curl -X PUT http://localhost:3000/books/1 \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "The Great Gatsby (Updated)",
    "author": "F. Scott Fitzgerald",
    "genre": "Classic Fiction",
    "publishedYear": 1925,
    "rating": 4.6
  }'
```

### DELETE /books/:id — Delete a book

```bash
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/3
```

### GET /stats — Get collection statistics

```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/stats
```

