        -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -d '{"title":"1984","author":"George Orwell","genre":"Dystopian","publishedYear":1949,"rating":4.7}'

   # Update a book
   curl -X PUT http://localhost:3000/api/books/6 \
        -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -d '{"title":"1984 (Updated)","author":"George Orwell","genre":"Dystopian","publishedYear":1949,"rating":4.8}'

   # Delete a book
   curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/books/6
   ```

---

## Summary of Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|----------|-----------|
| **In-memory array** | Simplest possible data store for learning; easy to inspect and modify |
| **Separate `data.js`** | Separates business logic from HTTP concerns, enabling future database swaps |
| **Custom error shape `{success, error}`** | Consistent API contract that clients can reliably parse |
| **HTTP status codes (201, 204, 400, 404)** | Follows REST conventions so the API behaves predictably |
| **`express.Router()`** | Enables modular route organization — critical for scaling to large apps |
| **Input validation in routes** | Fails fast with clear error messages before touching the data layer |
| **JSDoc on every function** | Self-documenting code that IDEs can render as hover tooltips |

This API is intentionally verbose and well-commented so you can read through it line by line and understand *why* each piece exists, not just *what* it does.

# API REST de Livros — Node.js + Express.js

Abaixo está uma implementação educacional completa de uma API REST para gerenciamento de livros. Cada arquivo é acompanhado de explicações detalhadas sobre as escolhas de design, padrões adotados e fundamentos teóricos por trás de cada decisão. A arquitetura segue o princípio de separação de responsabilidades (separation of concerns), mantendo rotas, modelos e middleware em arquivos distintos para facilitar a manutenção e escalabilidade futura.

